= Program (computing) — Simple =

A '''computer program''' is something written or stored so a computer can carry out a set of behaviors.

A program may be source code that people can read, or it may have been translated into machine code, bytecode, or another form.

A program is not exactly the same as an [[Algorithm/Simple|algorithm]]. The algorithm is the method. The program is an expression of behavior that a computing system can run or interpret.

It is also not the same as [[Software/Simple|software]]. A software system may contain many programs, libraries, configuration files, data, and other parts.

When a stored program is running, the running instance has its own current state and resources. This is often called a '''process'''.

Programs are commonly written in a [[Programming language/Simple|programming language]]. They may then be compiled, interpreted, or run by a virtual machine or other runtime.

